    {
      "id": "PsGCmf5rryfDVExsd0Bo7",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1031.5277917665478,
      "y": 1339.115704492242,
      "width": 1007.1452026367188,
      "height": 1661.2211967561796,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": "9FhZ4RGW18Bv99FUHTiU9",
      "index": "b06zzzzt",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1411034107,
      "version": 2749,
      "versionNonce": 384522905,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1774456554527,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Qt :\n    why we need a single source of truth why we don't just use a single table from one side ?\n    * raison n1:\n        so we can get the department of each employee with his email at the same time   \n    * raison n2 :\n    (for the ) so we can search when the employee didn't clock_in or clock_out if he is\n         working at home ( remote )\n            or\n         on a mission ( on custommer side )\n           or\n         he is really absent\n\nProblem :\ncan't find a single source of truth to combine the two tables why :\n    - Sometimes the biotime table does not have an email address for an employee\n     -> email == null\n      but sometimes u can find it on the tables of easyproject\n \n    - Biotime emp_ID != Easyproject user_id  \n    \n    - sometime the employee is on easyproject and have an email but on biotime he don't have an email\n    \nconclusion :\n    we don't have a single source of truth to get the same employee from the \n    biotime table and EasyProject except his first_name\n    + last_name  \n\nsolution :\n    \n    step 1 : first select employees from easyProject WITH their mails \n            \n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n\n\n    step2 : select employees with their department\n\n\n\n                \n\n    \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    at the end concatenate the View_Employee from biotime and easy_project and insert them into the \n    EMPLOYEE TABLE OF THE MAIN APP\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 19.83547697619319,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Qt :\n    why we need a single source of truth why we don't just use a single table from one side ?\n    * raison n1:\n        so we can get the department of each employee with his email at the same time   \n    * raison n2 :\n    (for the ) so we can search when the employee didn't clock_in or clock_out if he is\n         working at home ( remote )\n            or\n         on a mission ( on custommer side )\n           or\n         he is really absent\n\nProblem :\ncan't find a single source of truth to combine the two tables why :\n    - Sometimes the biotime table does not have an email address for an employee\n     -> email == null\n      but sometimes u can find it on the tables of easyproject\n \n    - Biotime emp_ID != Easyproject user_id  \n    \n    - sometime the employee is on easyproject and have an email but on biotime he don't have an email\n    \nconclusion :\n    we don't have a single source of truth to get the same employee from the \n    biotime table and EasyProject except his first_name\n    + last_name  \n\nsolution :\n    \n    step 1 : first select employees from easyProject WITH their mails \n            \n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n\n\n    step2 : select employees with their department\n\n\n\n                \n\n    \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    at the end concatenate the View_Employee from biotime and easy_project and insert them into the \n    EMPLOYEE TABLE OF THE MAIN APP\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
